# Drafted by Gemini (R11c gus), edited.

~ body
Narrator: Ned Cooper the woodcutter lies among the roots of the Oak of Many Faces, his head set neatly by his boots. Above the sated soil, the bark's carved faces glisten dark and wet.
quest gory_gus body
-> doris_scene

~ doris_scene
doris_squire [weary]: Ned Cooper. Taken the old way, just like Gus Strong used to do.
Narrator: The constable's pale eyes fix on your travel-stained cloaks.
doris_squire [neutral]: No killers left in this village. Only four strangers.
set gus_accused
* [Persuasion DC 14] Say we were at the inn all night -> cleared_ok | cleared_fail
* Offer to help find the killer -> help
* Ask what she found -> doris_found

~ cleared_ok
doris_squire [neutral]: Hmph. Barmaid's word holds weight. Stay out of trouble, or find me a better suspect.
quest gory_gus clues
-> END

~ cleared_fail
doris_squire [angry]: Inn doors have latches that lift both ways. I am watching you four.
quest gory_gus clues
-> END

~ help
doris_squire [weary]: Do what you like. Check the undertaker's table, or the carpentry shop. Just bring me truth.
quest gory_gus clues
-> END

~ doris_found
doris_squire [neutral]: Heavy woodman's axe. One clean stroke through the neck. Neat work, no struggle.
-> doris_scene

~ mori
if flag.gus_clue_hair
mori_shade [neutral]: The dead speak only once, travelers. Here is all poor Ned brought to my table.
-> END
endif
mori_shade [sad]: When I pried poor Ned's cold fingers open, I found this coarse grey hair, long as a widow's shawl.
set gus_clue_hair
mori_shade [neutral]: Look upon his palm: two tiny crossed axes seared into the flesh. The mark of Gus Strong's apprentice.
set gus_clue_hare
-> END

~ beatrice
beatrice_wells [smile]: Oh, a clean single stroke? That sounds like my heavy felling iron, fresh off the grindstone!
beatrice_wells [sad]: Sold one two nights past to Marta Dunn, a quiet widow in black. Said her hearthwood was terribly knotted.
set gus_clue_axe
-> END

~ marta
Narrator: The damp churchyard smells of turned earth and cold iron. Marta Dunn rests her hands on a broad, gleaming felling axe.
marta_dunn [sad]: Do not fret for Ned, my dears. Gus taught me a swift, kind stroke, so the old oak never thirsts.
* [Insight DC 14] Tell her we know her mark -> marta_know | marta_flat
* Draw weapons -> marta_fight
* Ask her to come quietly -> marta_quiet

~ marta_know
marta_dunn [smile]: Sharp eyes, youngsters. I kept Gus's brand and his duty. Wickermoor forgot its debts to the roots, so someone must pay the tally.
-> marta_fight_prompt

~ marta_flat
marta_dunn [smile]: An old widow has many chores in a cold season, my dears. Pay no mind to my hands.
-> marta

~ marta_quiet
marta_dunn [weary]: Bless you for asking kindly. Give myself to Doris's rope while the roots are still dry? No, my dears, the work is not half done.
-> marta_fight_prompt

~ marta_fight_prompt
Narrator: She lifts the heavy axe with practiced grace, her eyes steady and full of quiet pity.
* Fight -> marta_fight

~ marta_fight
quest gory_gus marta
combat wm_gus_marta

~ solved
quest gory_gus solved
set gus_solved
doris_squire [weary]: Marta Dunn. Never said three words a week. Good work, strangers. You are clear.
-> END
